<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Virumaa</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1220 CE (approx.) · capital Agelinde</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">North-eastern Estonian county on the Gulf of Finland, conquered by Denmark around 1220 and long a frontier facing Novgorod.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Virumaa, Vironia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, stretched along <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia's</a> northern coast towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narva">Narva</a> river. It was one of the largest ancient Estonian lands, with several parishes and hillforts; its main stronghold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rakvere">Agelinde</a>, is usually identified with Rakvere.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Elders led the county's parishes, and its coast gave access to trade with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-duchy-of-finland">Finland</a> and Novgorod. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-of-livonia">Henry of Livonia</a> records that Virumaa's elders submitted and accepted baptism under pressure from both the Germans and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a>, who competed for the land.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Virumaa passed under Danish rule after 1220, confirmed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-stensby">Treaty of Stensby</a> in 1238, and formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-estonia-1219-1346">Duchy of Estonia</a> (1219-1346). Novgorod attacked it repeatedly, notably at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-wesenberg-1268">Battle of Wesenberg</a> in 1268. The region later belonged to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/livonian-order">Livonian Order</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/virumaa.jpg" alt="Virumaa" width="320" height="219"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. 藏骨集团 assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancient_Estonian_counties.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1220 CE (ap